fix round 1 (2026-11-20): test_verify_sources.RecordedRobotsPolicy.test_blocked_redirect_is_reported_and_not_retried
failure: sleep.assert_not_called() saw 44 calls (0.001, 0.002, 0.004, 0.008, 0.016, 0.032, then 0.05 caps; two sequences)
root cause: the test patches vs.time.sleep, i.e. the global stdlib time.sleep. cmd_detect -> report()
  probes pdftotext -v and tesseract --version via tool_version -> subprocess.run(timeout=...).
  CPython 3.13 subprocess.Popen._wait busy-polls with delay=min(delay*2, .05) starting at 0.001
  (/usr/lib/python3.13/subprocess.py:2060). Under load the two tool children outlive the first
  waitpid poll, so their busy-wait sleeps are recorded by the test's mock: one backoff sequence
  per tool. Not a fetch retry; the fetch path itself never slept (opener.open called once).
repro (deterministic): PATH shims for pdftotext/tesseract that emit version output, close
  stdout/stderr, then linger 0.3s force the communicate() -> wait() busy-poll window.
  Pre-fix test body under the shims: sleep.call_count=138030, first calls exactly
  [0.001, 0.002, 0.004, 0.008, 0.016, 0.032, 0.05, 0.05, ...] — diagnosis confirmed.
fix: mock vs.tool_version (return None) in the test, the same convention as
  test_verify_sources_fetch.py run_detect; no subprocess runs inside the patched window.
  Fixed test under the same shims: OK (0.002s). No production code changed.
